# A real environment file points at a real deployment, and the first person to
# do that would otherwise commit its address by habit. `.env.example` is the
# committed template and is deliberately not ignored — it is the file a reader
# copies, so it has to be in the tree.
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
